# Dataspace participation agreement

**{{ project.name }} dataspace, {{ dataspace.short }} pilot — version {{ doc.version }}**

## 1. Purpose

This agreement governs an organisation's participation in the {{ project.name }} dataspace for the
{{ dataspace.short }} pilot. In the dataspace, admitted parties obtain two kinds of data relating to the
members of a renewable energy community:

- metering data;
- energy data derived from it.

They obtain it only under the sharing offers published in the dataspace, and only on
the basis of those members' decisions.

The {{ project.name }} project is funded by the European Union under the {{ project.programme }} programme,
grant agreement No. {{ project.grant_agreement }}.

## 2. Accepting the agreement

An organisation participates once it has accepted this version of the agreement through
the dataspace's identity registry. The registry records:

- who accepted, when, and in which language;
- the fingerprint of the text accepted.

Only an organisation that has accepted the agreement receives the credentials needed to
take part.

## 3. Capacity

The participating organisation acts as an **independent controller**. It determines the
purposes for which it processes the data it receives. Consequently:

- it is not covered by a disclosure made about another party;
- each member's decision is sought for it in its own right, for each purpose it takes
  part in.

An organisation that processes data on behalf of another party accepts a separate
agreement stating that capacity.

## 4. Operation of the dataspace

{{ platform.name }} operates each participant's dataspace node on that participant's
behalf. This covers the connector, the identity and the consent record. {{ platform.short }}
acts as processor under a data processing agreement with each participant.

The dataspace runs on infrastructure in the European Economic Area:

- {{ providers.hosting.brand }}, in the European Union;
- {{ platform.short }}{{ "'" if platform.short.endswith('s') else "'s" }} own infrastructure in {{ platform.city }}, {{ platform.country.en }}.

## 5. Obligations

Each participating organisation:

- **Purpose:** processes data only for the purposes declared in the sharing offers to
  which it has been admitted, and only for as long as it is admitted.
- **Withdrawal:** honours every withdrawal of a member's decision.
  - It obtains nothing further for that member from the moment the withdrawal is
    recorded.
  - It leaves the member out of every export and every new processing within 7 days.
- **Retention:** keeps member-level data no longer than the retention each offer
  declares.
- **Security:** maintains technical and organisational security measures appropriate to
  energy consumption data, which can reveal household behaviour.
- **Assistance:** assists the other participants in meeting data-subject requests.
- **Breaches:** notifies the participants concerned of a personal-data breach affecting
  data obtained in the dataspace within 48 hours of becoming aware of it.
- **Onward disclosure:** discloses data onward only to a party that has itself accepted
  an agreement in this dataspace, and only where a sharing offer admits it.

## 6. Provenance and evidence

Each disclosure is recorded in the dataspace, per supply point, with the date of the
member's decision.

- **What a participant relies on:** that record, as its evidence of the basis for
  obtaining the data.
- **What is not evidence:** the presence of a supply point in a list is never a basis
  in itself.

## 7. Term and versions

This agreement applies for the duration of the {{ project.name }} pilot.

A new version of the agreement:

- replaces this one only for an organisation that accepts it;
- is never carried forward by the acceptance of an earlier version.

An organisation that does not accept a new version stops receiving data under it.

## 8. Law and disputes

This agreement is governed by Italian law. The courts of {{ dataspace.forum.en }} have exclusive
jurisdiction over any dispute arising from it.
